    <GaugingStation location="Kedington" name="Stour" number="36012">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Insensitive 'Essex' profile gauging a small, rural, Chalk catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Insensitive. High downstream levels make estimate of flow peak uncertain. Ponding u/s above 11.5 cumecs. Rating above bank full tends to overestimate flows. Crest tapping prone to siltation which made modular limit uncertain until 1970, when channel improved for Ely/Ouse Transfer Scheme, making station full range. Structure built on peat, some percolation beneath. Adjustments have been to flows to account for non-modularity. One rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">'Essex' profile (modified Flat V Crump) weir with crest tapping. No spillway.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Station was completely overwhelmed in Sept 1968 floods, which is the highest event on record. Post 1976 adjustments made for Ely/Ouse Transfer Scheme. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Gw-influenced regime. Effect of Transfer Scheme results in unrealistic water balance. Abstraction from surface water and gw for industrial/agricultural purposes. Runoff increased by effluent returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Boulder Clay overlying Chalk, some outcropping. Rural, predominantly arable land.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">RGEI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Good fit to gaugings." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Although gauged to within 16% of AMAX3, rating above bankfull overestimates flows and extrapolation is highly uncertain." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
